course: dictionary
lesson: 13764
title: Formal words: interred
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound serious and belong in special places, such as history books, churches and old gravestones. «Here lies interred a brave soldier» is a formal way of saying that a soldier is buried in this spot.
explain: Interred means buried. A person who is interred has been placed in a grave or tomb after they die. The clues around it help: «here lies», a stone, and a grave all point to burial.
explain: Interred is the past tense of inter. You may also see it with a helper word, as in «was interred at» or «interred in».
fact: Interred means buried, and it is a formal, respectful word.
fact: Interred is the past tense of inter: inter, inters, interred, interring.
fact: «Here lies interred» is often carved on old gravestones and church plaques.
fact: Interred can also mean placed in a tomb, vault or urn, which are all burial places.
fact: In a churchyard, ashes may be interred, which means they are buried there.
exercise: «The king was interred in the great stone tomb.» What does interred mean here? | *Buried | Painted | Crowned | Carried
exercise: Which phrase might you read carved on an old gravestone? | *Here lies interred | Happy birthday to you | Let's go to the park | Dinner is served
exercise: Ben says interred means dug up. What does interred really mean? | Painted bright red | Dug up from the ground | Stolen by thieves | *Buried in a grave
test: «His remains were interred in the churchyard last spring.» What does interred mean? | Left on a sunny beach | Lit up with lights | *Put in the ground for burial | Taken to school for a show
test: Which word is the past tense of inter? | interring | interrupted | *interred | inters
exam: «Her grandmother was interred at the old village church.» What does interred mean in this sentence? | *Buried | Painted | Married | Visited
